        <h1 class="post-detail__title">COVID-19: Foundation Update</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/47045.webp" alt="COVID-19: Foundation Update" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <div aria-hidden="true">

<p>Dear Teton Valley,</p>

<p>In response to COVID-19 and the recommendations made through the Center for Disease Control regarding COVID-19 best practices “Community Mitigation Strategies,” the Community Foundation of Teton Valley will be closing our office to the public beginning Monday, March 16<sup>th</sup>.&nbsp;&nbsp;Staff will be working from home until April 20<sup>th</sup>, at which time we will reassess the situation.&nbsp;&nbsp;All Foundation business will continue as normal until our return to the office.&nbsp;&nbsp;Emails will be addressed and phone calls will be returned in a timely manner.&nbsp;&nbsp;Mail will be collected on a daily basis and any correspondence will be attended to.</p>

<p>Where possible we will change our in-person meetings and workshops to video or conference calls.&nbsp;&nbsp;Should that not be available, we will work to reschedule those meetings or workshops at a later date.</p>

<p>Tuesday, March 17<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;is our Tin Cup Kick-off Meeting and the opening of the Tin Cup Application Period.&nbsp;&nbsp;This meeting has been moved to a video conference format.&nbsp;&nbsp;At this time, there are no changes to the 2020 Annual Tin Cup Challenge.&nbsp;&nbsp;All timelines and efforts associated with the Tin Cup will move forward as planned.&nbsp;&nbsp;Should circumstances arise that necessitate changes or alterations to the Tin Cup Challenge, the Foundation will communicate those broadly to Teton Valley nonprofits and supporters.</p>

<p>The Community Foundation of Teton Valley will work to assist our nonprofits as best we can in these trying times.&nbsp;&nbsp;We are a close-knit family of nonprofits and leaning on each other for support will no doubt help bolster us as we move through the next few months.&nbsp;&nbsp;I am certain we will be stronger as we emerge on the other side.</p>

<p>Please do not hesitate to reach out with any questions.</p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Tim Adams<br>Executive Director<br>Community Foundation of Teton Valley</p>

